# Agent Action Firewall — Cursor context

You are helping build Agent Action Firewall (AAF), a runtime protection layer
for AI agent actions. Read this file fully before any work in this repo.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## What this project is

AAF is a runtime interception layer that sits between any AI agent and the
external systems it can manipulate (email, social networks, databases, APIs,
files, payment services). It inspects, classifies, and authorizes every
action before execution.

The product solves a real, documented problem: agents that go runaway and
cause irreversible damage (e.g., the OpenClaw incident in Feb 2026 where an
agent deleted an entire Gmail inbox despite stop commands; the LangChain
$47K loop incident in Nov 2025).

Current alternatives in the market (Galileo, Lakera, NeMo Guardrails) filter
text input/output of LLMs. They do NOT intervene at the action layer. AAF
fills that gap.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## Project status

Pre-alpha. Core firewall (5-layer pipeline) and CLI policy validation are implemented. Learning Mode, wrappers, and Slack channel are pending.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## Architecture in one paragraph

AAF wraps an agent's tools with a 5-layer pipeline:
1. Intent Classifier — risk tier (R1–R4)
2. Rate Limiter & Budget Tracker
3. Behavioral Anomaly Detector (repetition, loops, velocity, mass actions)
4. Approval Gate (tier-based human-in-the-loop)
5. Kill Switch & Immutable Audit Log (Ed25519 signed)

Target total latency: under 200ms at p95.

